  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Suresh Mulchand Agrawal vs The State Of Maharashtra on 6 June, 2019 Author: Sarang V. Kotwal Bench: Sarang V. Kotwal 1/4 916-ABA-1167-19.odt In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No.1167 Of 2019 Suresh Mulchand Agrawal .... Applicant versus The State of Maharashtra .... Respondent ....... Mr.Prashant Pandey i/b. Pradeep D. Singh, Advocate for Applicant. Mr.Deepak Thakare, Pp, a/w Ms.Sharmila Kaushik, App for the State/Respondent. Api Mr.A.G. More, Chandan Nagar Police Station, Pune, present. Coram : Sarang V. Kotwal, J. Date : 06th June, 2019 P.C. : 1. The Applicant is seeking anticipatory bail in connection with C.R.No.186/19 registered with Chandan Nagar Police Station, Pune, under sections 188, 272, 279 and 328 of the Indian Penal Code. 2 . The FIR is lodged on 30/04/2019 by the Food Safety Nesarikar Suresh Mulchand Agrawal vs The State Of Maharashtra on 6 June, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/50335892/ 1 ::: Uploaded on - 06/06/2019 ::: Downloaded on - 07/06/2019 04:38:3 2/4 916-ABA-1167-19.odt Officer, Ms. Shubhangi Balkrushna Ankush.",
    "facts": "According to her, API Chandan Nagar Police Station informed the Food Inspectors on 24/03/2019 itself that a worker of a political party drove a car belonging to the present Applicant to Kharadi Police Chowky. However, the letter was given on 30/04/2019 and goods in the car were seized on 30/04/2019. The goods contained a large quantity of Pan Masala, Tobacco, Gutkha etc. which were banned substances under the orders passed by the Commissioner appointed under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. The car and the goods were seized on 30/04/2019. According to the prosecution, the car was taken charge of on 24/03/2019 and was kept in the police station for more than a month without any Panchanama or any protection of the goods kept in the car. It is very difficult to understand why the police had shown such gross negligence in investigating the Suresh Mulchand Agrawal vs The State Of Maharashtra on 6 June, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/50335892/ 2 offence. It is very difficult to connect the seized goods with the present Applicant, if the goods were seized after one month of keeping vehicle in the police station.",
